{
  "name": "Weekly broken-link report to Google Sheets with email alert (Apify)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d1900e9c-8f65-4670-989d-63e6a9ccac62",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -420,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 440,
        "height": 720,
        "content": "## Weekly broken-link report with email alert\n\n**Who it's for:** site owners, SEO consultants and agencies who want to catch 404s and dead links before visitors and search engines do.\n\n**How it works**\n1. Every Monday at 8:00 the workflow reads your settings (sites, page limit, alert email).\n2. It crawls each site with the Broken Link Checker Actor on Apify, checking internal pages and outbound links.\n3. Results are split: each broken link becomes a clean row appended to Google Sheets, building a weekly history.\n4. The per-site summaries are combined; if any broken links were found, you get one email with the totals per site and a link to the sheet. Clean weeks send nothing.\n\n**Setup (10 min)**\n1. Create a free Apify account. In **Crawl sites with Apify** add an *HTTP Header Auth* credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n2. Edit **Settings**: your sites, `maxPagesPerSite`, alert email and sheet URL.\n3. In **Append broken links to sheet** connect Google Sheets and pick a sheet with headers: checkedAt, site, brokenUrl, statusCode, error, linkType, foundOnPage, anchorText.\n4. In **Email the weekly summary** connect Gmail (or swap for Slack/Outlook).\n\n**Cost:** Apify charges per page crawled, about $1.50 per 1,000 pages; `maxTotalChargeUsd=2` caps each run at $2."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5d244447-b576-41d0-81ca-ea65a4f63bc1",
      "name": "Section: crawl",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        160,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "### 1. Settings and crawl\nOne place to change sites and limits. The HTTP node calls Apify's run-sync endpoint, so the whole crawl happens in one request (up to 5 min).",
        "color": "5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "01593b97-472e-4616-abb9-521ea6ce9638",
      "name": "Section: report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        740,
        -120
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "### 2. Log and alert\nTop branch: one row per broken link in Google Sheets.\nBottom branch: totals per site, then an email only when something is broken.",
        "color": "6"
      }
    },
